$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/amazon-fantasy-companion-technical-plan.md:119:| AC-AFC-D5-01 | The Alphazedehq repository shall contain one shared skill `skills/spec-authoring/` holding a `SKILL.md` within skill_size_max, a specification template, and build, lint and diagram scripts that run with `uv run --script` (PEP 723 inline dependencies) and Graphviz `dot`, without any project-specific Python environment, and shall retain the GridMarket MIT copyright and permission notice. | SD-022, C10, `create-lean-skill` | test, inspection | S06; D5 skill directory |
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/amazon-fantasy-companion-technical-plan.md:120:| AC-AFC-D5-02 | The spec-authoring skill’s operational text, templates and tool invocation shall contain no GridMarket product name, document id or `--project backend` flag; GridMarket references shall occur only in retained license, attribution and provenance records, and the skill shall contain no absolute local path; building and linting its shipped template in a temporary directory outside any git repository shall exit 0. | SD-022 ("nothing GridMarket-specific"), SD-019, C7 | test | S06; D5 skill directory |
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/amazon-fantasy-companion-technical-plan.md:121:| AC-AFC-D5-03 | The spec-authoring skill description shall name SDoc and Requirements System documents as non-triggers and shall cite `requirements-engineering` by reference without restating its checklist, so that a request to author and build a Markdown specification selects spec-authoring and a request to publish an SDoc revision to the Requirements System selects `use-requirements-system`. | `create-lean-skill`, C10 | test, inspection | S06; D5 skill description |
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/amazon-fantasy-companion-technical-plan.md:122:| AC-AFC-D5-04 | The skill's vendor step shall copy its scripts to `<repo>/tools/spec/` with a `VENDORED.md` naming the source repository, commit and MIT notice, and shall refuse to overwrite a vendored copy whose files differ from that recorded commit. | SD-022, SD-010 | test | S06; D5 vendor script |
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/amazon-fantasy-companion-technical-plan.md:123:| AC-AFC-D5-05 | The program shall land the spec-authoring skill in Alphazedehq through its own pull request merged by rebase or merge commit, shall then link it into every harness skill directory that already links the shared skills, and shall have the D4 hook installer link it for the remaining harnesses of SD-021 or record each as a typed gap. | SD-022, workspace rule (never squash), coverage ledger (Muse skills gap) | inspection | S06 (PR), S06L (links), S11 (Muse/AGY links or typed gaps) |
