$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:2985:          "S06L",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:2994:        "compared": "The technical plan §Program plan ('one review per Phase 1 pull request at the phase boundary') and DES-AFC-LANES Landing ('reviewed once at the Phase 1 boundary') put every review at the single Phase 1 boundary. Merge needs that review (AC-AFC-LAND-01). But the Wave 2 edges need merges inside Phase 1: S06->S42 ('S06 merged'), S42->S09T, S09->S11, S09->S08, and C13 for S11T. Read literally, no Wave 2 slice can start until Phase 1 ends, and Phase 1 cannot end without them.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3002:          "S06L",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3006:        "compared": "S06L lease 'harness-configs, alphazedehq-main-checkout' and S42 lease 'alphazedehq-main-checkout'. Both only read the checkout, and both dispatch on the S06 merge. Because DES-AFC-LANES grants each lease 'to one slice at a time', they serialize for no reason. Separately, 'fast-forward only, between dispatches' does not stop a fast-forward while Wave 1 or Wave 2 sessions run: under continuous dispatch, merges always land while other sessions are running. The S03 fast-forward changes ship-pull-request for every PR-opening session on the host.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3008:        "corrected_text": "- `alphazedehq-main-checkout`: a reader-writer lease. Slices that read skills from the checkout (S06L, S42) and the IE-P1-10 live install hold a shared read lease. The Orchestrator's fast-forward (CMD-AZHQ-SYNC) takes it exclusively. It runs only when no read lease is held and no session of this Lifecycle is opening or landing a pull request. Each sync records the HEAD before and after it and the sessions running at that moment. The HEAD is recorded in each later packet."
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3014:          "S06",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3018:        "compared": "CONTRACT-AFC-SPECKIT vendor step ('copies the scripts to <repo root>/tools/spec/') and DES-AFC-D5 references/vendoring.md ('copy scripts/') vs DES-AFC-GATE spec area ('copies tools/spec/template/ into a temporary directory', AC-AFC-CI-04). The template is never vendored. S42 stop condition 'VENDORED.md names the merged D5 commit': vendor.sh runs from the live main checkout, which may already be past the D5 merge, so the commit it records is undefined.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3019:        "target": "design.md §Contracts CONTRACT-AFC-SPECKIT, vendor bullet; design.md DES-AFC-D5 files table, references/vendoring.md row; slice-graph.md S42 Stop condition",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3020:        "corrected_text": "CONTRACT-AFC-SPECKIT: '- `<skill>/scripts/vendor.sh <repo root>` — copies the contents of `scripts/` and the `template/` directory to `<repo root>/tools/spec/` (template at `tools/spec/template/`) and writes `VENDORED.md` (source repository; source commit = `git log -1 --format=%H -- <skill dir>` in the source checkout; the tree id of the skill directory at that commit; MIT notice); refuses to run when the skill directory has uncommitted changes, and refuses to overwrite a vendored copy whose files differ from its recorded commit.' vendoring.md row: 'When a repository's CI cannot reach the shared skill (private skill, public repository): copy `scripts/` and `template/` to `<repo>/tools/spec/` with `scripts/vendor.sh`, which writes `VENDORED.md` (source commit, skill tree id, MIT notice).' S42 Stop condition: '`tools/spec/VENDORED.md` names a source commit whose `skills/spec-authoring/` tree id equals that of the merged D5 commit; vendored files (scripts and template) equal that tree; MIT notice present in both files.'"
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3041:        "corrected_text": "S11 Depends on: `S11T, S09 merged, S06 merged, S06L, S41 merged when OD-AFC-01 = B`. Dependencies list add: `S41 --> S11 (only when OD-AFC-01 = B)`."
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3059:          "S06L"
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3061:        "compared": "S06L writes docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/evidence/skill-links.txt in this repository. DES-AFC-LANES Landing lists PRs only for S07, S42, S09 and S08, so S06L's evidence has no landing path.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3063:        "corrected_text": "- This repository: one pull request each for S07, S06L (link readback evidence), S42, S09 (tests and gate) and S08."
